@startuml SecureAccountPortal
' Assignment 7, Q2: Security use case overview diagram (UML) with misuse management
' System: Secure Account Portal (the account application built in Project 1)
' Notation follows Richardson and Thies (2012), Chapters 7 and 8:
'   [E] crosses the external system boundary   [I] internal, host-to-host
'   [C] carries critical or sensitive data      [A] potential attack point
'   Normal operation on the left, security operation and the attacker on the right
' Author: Ananya Solanki, Secure Software Development, Fall 2026

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 18
skinparam ranksep 70
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #333333
  BackgroundColor<<security>> #DDEBF7
  BorderColor<<security>> #2F5597
  BackgroundColor<<misuse>> #262626
  FontColor<<misuse>> #FFFFFF
  BorderColor<<misuse>> #000000
  StereotypeFontColor<<misuse>> #FFFFFF
}

title Secure Account Portal: Use Case Overview with Security and Misuse Cases

actor "Customer" as Customer
actor "Bank\nAdministrator" as Admin
actor "Compliance\nAuditor" as Auditor

rectangle "Secure Account Portal (system and trust boundary)" {
  usecase "UC1 Log In" as UC1
  usecase "UC3 Transfer Funds" as UC3
  usecase "UC4 Manage User Roles" as UC4
  usecase "UC2 View Account Balance" as UC2
  usecase "UC5 Review Audit Log" as UC5

  usecase "S1 Verify Second\nFactor (TOTP)" as S1 <<security>>
  usecase "S2 Lock Account After\n5 Failed Attempts" as S2 <<security>>
  usecase "S4 Validate and\nParameterize Input" as S4 <<security>>
  usecase "S3 Enforce Role-Based\nAuthorization" as S3 <<security>>
  usecase "S6 Record Audit Event" as S6 <<security>>
  usecase "S5 Encrypt Session\n(TLS 1.3)" as S5 <<security>>

  usecase "M1 Stuff or Guess\nPasswords" as M1 <<misuse>>
  usecase "M3 Inject SQL" as M3 <<misuse>>
  usecase "M2 Escalate Privilege" as M2 <<misuse>>
  usecase "M4 Hijack Session" as M4 <<misuse>>
}

actor "Attacker" as Attacker
actor "Account Database\n(existing system)" as DB

' Legitimate actors (normal operation)
Customer --> UC1 : [E][C][A]
Customer --> UC3 : [E][C][A]
Customer --> UC2 : [E][C]
Admin --> UC1 : [E][C][A]
Admin --> UC4 : [E][C][A]
Auditor --> UC5 : [E][C]

' Security use cases built into normal operation
UC1 ..> S1 : <<include>>
S2 .> UC1 : <<extend>>
UC1 ..> S5 : <<include>>
UC3 ..> S4 : <<include>>
UC3 ..> S3 : <<include>>
UC3 ..> S6 : <<include>>
UC4 ..> S3 : <<include>>
UC4 ..> S6 : <<include>>
UC2 ..> S3 : <<include>>
UC5 ..> S3 : <<include>>

' Security operation: controls against attacker goals
S1 ..> M1 : MITIGATES
S2 ..> M1 : MITIGATES
S4 ..> M3 : MITIGATES
S3 ..> M2 : MITIGATES
S6 ..> M2 : DETECTS
S5 ..> M4 : MITIGATES

' Attacker goals threaten business use cases
UC1 <.... M1 : THREATENS
UC3 <.... M3 : THREATENS
UC4 <.... M2 : THREATENS
UC2 <.... M4 : THREATENS

M1 <-- Attacker : [E][A]
M3 <-- Attacker : [E][A]
M2 <-- Attacker : [E][A]
M4 <-- Attacker : [E][A]

S4 ---> DB : [I][C]
S6 ---> DB : [I][C]

legend right
  White: business use cases (normal operation)
  Blue <<security>>: security use cases
  Black <<misuse>>: misuse cases (attacker goals)
  [E] external boundary   [I] internal link
  [C] critical data       [A] attack point
  ----
  Fail case exit states
  Login fails: generic "invalid credentials" only,
    no remaining-attempt count shown
  Role check fails: HTTP 403, no data, event logged
  Input rejected: refused before any query runs
  TLS fails: connection closed, nothing sent in clear
endlegend
@enduml
